{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01073",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 6.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Hi, um, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.17,
      "end_seconds": 12.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.76,
      "end_seconds": 25.95,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "Hello, uh, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this. Ah, um, we came because of skipped beats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.17,
      "end_seconds": 33.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "when did this begin? These questions might sound routine, but they matter"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.85,
      "end_seconds": 38.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Ah, I've had it since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.52,
      "end_seconds": 43.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Right, how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.98,
      "end_seconds": 45.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.03,
      "end_seconds": 48.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "have you tried anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.45,
      "end_seconds": 52.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Yeah, deep breaths helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.59,
      "end_seconds": 60.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.53,
      "end_seconds": 67.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.49,
      "end_seconds": 71.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Is anything making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.47,
      "end_seconds": 95.94,
      "duration_seconds": 22.47,
      "text": "Right, I notice it more with caffeine and lying down. As for flutter in my chest, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. And being a bit anxious, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.31,
      "end_seconds": 100.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Did you notice any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.12,
      "end_seconds": 104.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Nope, no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.47,
      "end_seconds": 109.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "have you had any chest pain or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.74,
      "end_seconds": 115.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "No, um, no chest pain or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 118.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "nothing like dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.36,
      "end_seconds": 120.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Definitely no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 121.55,
      "end_seconds": 128.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "Actually, um, doctor, I did notice dizziness. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.98,
      "end_seconds": 137.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.78,
      "end_seconds": 145.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.21,
      "end_seconds": 148.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.88,
      "end_seconds": 152.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.5,
      "end_seconds": 165.6,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I had a reaction to trimethoprim when I was younger, itching, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.41,
      "end_seconds": 169.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.07,
      "end_seconds": 178.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "Yes, eczema. My family kept telling me to get it checked. Gout, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.54,
      "end_seconds": 180.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.12,
      "end_seconds": 190.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Okay, I can see gout in your file as well. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.56,
      "end_seconds": 193.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.44,
      "end_seconds": 197.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 198.46,
      "end_seconds": 215.67,
      "duration_seconds": 17.21,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so she is on hydrocortisone cream, when needed, I give it to her. She takes febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day. She takes herbal calming tea, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.76,
      "end_seconds": 218.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.98,
      "end_seconds": 222.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.79,
      "end_seconds": 225.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Okay, do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.02,
      "end_seconds": 233.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.49,
      "end_seconds": 237.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.12,
      "end_seconds": 243.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.93,
      "end_seconds": 246.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.57,
      "end_seconds": 251.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.21,
      "end_seconds": 271.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.86,
      "end_seconds": 287.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.95,
      "end_seconds": 306.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "okay: pulse is 67 beats a minute, SpO2 99 percent on room air and pressure 124 over 71, temperature is 36.6 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.29,
      "end_seconds": 311.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.18,
      "end_seconds": 314.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.8,
      "end_seconds": 331.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.74,
      "end_seconds": 336.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.85,
      "end_seconds": 357.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, the most likely explanation is harmless extra heartbeats. I can't rule out an anxiety-related palpitation yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.65,
      "end_seconds": 361.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "is it it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.64,
      "end_seconds": 378.7,
      "duration_seconds": 16.06,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like harmless extra heartbeats, but I'd like to confirm. So, to recap quickly. You've had skipped beats, since this morning, moderate, and no fainting or shortness of breath"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.64,
      "end_seconds": 382.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.75,
      "end_seconds": 394.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Let's book an ECG to look into palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.71,
      "end_seconds": 402.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.63,
      "end_seconds": 410.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a diary of when it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.25,
      "end_seconds": 436.05,
      "duration_seconds": 24.8,
      "text": "right, right make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest do get help quickly if you faint or have chest pain come back if it carries on after a month right, that's the plan do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.91,
      "end_seconds": 440.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Uh, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}